text:
Score: 5/10.

The core client is small and readable, and the current test suite passes (`9 passed`). I would not approve it as-is. The biggest risks are unsafe URL construction, weak error/retry behavior, silent schema/data loss, and a “typed” model layer that does not validate several of its advertised types.

Estimated rewrite/significant-change size: about 180 LOC, mostly in `lumen/client.py`, `lumen/models.py`, and tests.

```json
{
  "score": 5,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "171-172, 193-196, 224, 239-242",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Resource IDs are interpolated into URL paths without percent-encoding, so slashes, query strings, or fragments can alter the requested endpoint."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "77-91",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "The retry loop handles only HTTP responses; timeouts and transport failures are not retried or wrapped in typed SDK errors."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "185-188",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "batch_create eagerly materializes the entire iterable, contradicting the documented any-number/any-iterable behavior and risking high memory use."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "164-167, 225-228",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Paginated list methods silently skip malformed items instead of raising schema errors, which can hide API corruption or data loss."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "198-200",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "batch_create silently drops malformed result entries and can return fewer results than requested without surfacing an error."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/models.py",
      "lines": "40-56, 85-98, 129-145, 148-164",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Literal-backed fields such as status, state, batch status, and verdict are not runtime-validated, so invalid API states enter typed models."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/models.py",
      "lines": "60-82, 85-103, 106-126, 148-164",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Frozen dataclasses expose mutable dict fields and return those dicts from to_dict, allowing model state to mutate after construction."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "81-82",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "HTTP 207 is treated as success for every endpoint instead of only the batch endpoint, which can bypass normal error handling."
    },
    {
      "file": "lumen/client.py",
      "lines": "43-47",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "max_attempts is not validated, so zero or negative values produce a misleading runtime failure instead of a configuration error."
    },
    {
      "file": "pyproject.toml",
      "lines": "24-25",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "The package advertises a typed client but does not ship a py.typed marker, so installed users may not get PEP 561 type information."
    }
  ],
  "lines_to_rewrite": 180,
  "approve": false
}
```
